Root cause:
The bug arises from the potential overflow of the `mmap_page` variable, which is limited to 32 bits. When inserting a new mmap entry, if the total number of pages exceeds this limit, it can lead to incorrect memory management and undefined behavior. The original code did not check for this overflow, making it susceptible to errors when handling large memory mappings.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
ucontext->mmap_xa_page += DIV_ROUND_UP(length, PAGE_SIZE);
```
```c
entry->mmap_page = ucontext->mmap_xa_page;
```
Reason:
The `mmap_xa_page` variable is incremented without checking if the addition would exceed the 32-bit limit. If the total number of pages exceeds this limit, it can lead to an overflow, resulting in incorrect memory management and undefined behavior when inserting a new mmap entry.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (check_add_overflow(ucontext->mmap_xa_page, (u32)(length >> PAGE_SHIFT), &next_mmap_page))
```
```c
ucontext->mmap_xa_page = next_mmap_page;
```
Reason:
The `check_add_overflow` function is introduced to verify if adding the new pages would exceed the 32-bit limit. If an overflow is detected, the function prevents the addition, thus ensuring safe memory management and avoiding undefined behavior when inserting a new mmap entry. The `next_mmap_page` variable is used to store the result of the safe addition, which is then assigned to `mmap_xa_page` only if no overflow occurs.


Now, determine whether the provided code snippet is buggy:
{
	struct efa_mmap_entry *entry;
	int err;

	entry = kmalloc(sizeof(*entry), GFP_KERNEL);
	if (!entry)
		return EFA_MMAP_INVALID;

	entry->obj = obj;
	entry->address = address;
	entry->length = length;
	entry->mmap_flag = mmap_flag;

	xa_lock(&ucontext->mmap_xa);
	entry->mmap_page = ucontext->mmap_xa_page;
	ucontext->mmap_xa_page += DIV_ROUND_UP(length, PAGE_SIZE);
	err = __xa_insert(&ucontext->mmap_xa, entry->mmap_page, entry,
			  GFP_KERNEL);
	xa_unlock(&ucontext->mmap_xa);
	if (err){
		kfree(entry);
		return EFA_MMAP_INVALID;
	}

	ibdev_dbg(
		&dev->ibdev,
		"mmap: obj[0x%p] addr[%#llx], len[%#llx], key[%#llx] inserted\n",
		entry->obj, entry->address, entry->length, get_mmap_key(entry));

	return get_mmap_key(entry);
}

